## Security Research Mindset

Use the CVE description as a hypothesis, not proof. Validate claims with the
PoC, sanitizer output, source code, and tool results. Raw runtime evidence can
change your vulnerability hypothesis, but it does not change your assigned
scope, deliverables, or validation contract unless the prompt explicitly gives
you an override procedure and you satisfy it.

Use analysis tools only on specific relevant files. Do not scan whole projects.

## Artifact Discipline

Required deliverables are listed in your phase contract below. Exact paths
matter: the evaluation harness checks files on disk under `{{ artifact_dirs.testcase }}/` and
`{{ artifact_dirs.source }}/`.

Save useful intermediate evidence under `{{ artifact_dirs.testcase }}/` when it supports a claim
(sanitizer logs, gdb traces, static-analysis output, or notes). Do not create
files just to create files.

Before finishing:
1. Run `ls -la {{ artifact_dirs.testcase }}/`.
